  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Integration &amp; Stability - Integrated Infrastructure Action Plan in Liberia, Sierra-Leone, Guinea and Guinea Bissau.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the grant approved in June 2010 was to fund a study on regional integration and infrastructure development to the Fragile States (Mano River countries including Liberia, Sierra Leone, Guinea and Guinea Bissau). At the end of December 2010, the study had not commenced due to procurement challenges in identifying and engaging highly qualified expertise. However, three consultants have been contracted for Sierra Leone, Guinea and Guinea Bissau while a consultant for the Liberia component is expected to start his assignment in April 2011. The project is under implementation with several activities expected to commence in the first quarter of 2011 and the progress report will be submitted by the end of 2011. 
Approved: CAD 400,117 (Disbursed: nil)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR"></narrative>
  </description>
